{
  "toolName": "ak_judge_output",
  "toolCallId": "call_mEk3g2zTeSnHVpotBjPGAMLY|fc_0ae31a6858351a3c016a6cb17947c081919d90fdbed794d8ad",
  "details": {
    "judgeStatus": "continue",
    "fix": {
      "summary": "The Authority subquestion is converged: R1 + L1 resolves the only owner-policy conflicts and no further authority decision or Plan is required. The separately requested direct-construction disposition remains `continue` because current HEAD still lacks the ratified Doctor v1 and StatsLine v1 package surfaces and retains pre-R1/L1 materials. Construct the seven bounded classes below directly; this does not condition Authority convergence on Apply evidence."
    },
    "classes": [
      {
        "name": "authority-contracts",
        "owner": "Issue #12 authority and docs/adr/0012-0014",
        "boundary": "The durable design boundary for Doctor and closure statistics; it records public role ownership and semantics but owns neither runtime mechanics nor host workflow topology.",
        "disposition": "Amend the Doctor authority materials forward to incorporate R1 and L1, then mark/preserve ADR 0012-0014 consistently with this ruling. R1 means `lastRealBite` is required and non-null but is a discriminated union: an actual docket Receipt/verdict citation, or a `noRealBite` branch proving a complete bounded search of the admitted population. The latter is never named or described as a bite. L1 means the four-reason rejection law remains solely caller/host overlay: do not put it, a paraphrase, or a package-invented canonical source in Doctor Soul, tool descriptions, output schema, or runtime. Preserve ADR 0012's evidence-only seat, ADR 0013's factory-only patient and five target kinds, ADR 0014's closure-produced single ledger, ADR 0010 caller-owned composition, manual v1 summoning, and README's usage-only status. Update CONTEXT only to distinguish actual bite from a no-bite proof and to reflect the finalized StatsLine meaning; do not turn glossary prose into a second contract."
      },
      {
        "name": "stats-line-v1",
        "owner": "A package-owned deterministic case-statistics contract and pure committed-snapshot producer",
        "boundary": "One per-case line derived at closure from a committed `.ak/dockets/issues/<n>/` population plus typed normalized tracker metadata. The caller invokes it and preserves its result in that same issue docket; Doctor only consumes preserved lines. It does not own closure scheduling, hooks, tracker querying, or another ledger.",
        "disposition": "Define a closed `StatsLineV1` contract with `version: 1`, exact `caseKey { repository, issueNumber }`, a source identity binding the full target commit and complete sorted manifest population, and these required metrics: `recordedInvocations { total, byRole, unclassified }`, `judgeContinueCount`, `auditRejectionCount`, `recordedInvocationWindow`, `issueToDefaultMerge`, `paperApplyBytes`, and `paperApplyWallClock`. Every metric whose value may not be proved is a typed `measured | unavailable` union with an enumerated reason; never use null, zero, Git commit time, prose, or an estimate to stand for unavailable evidence. At v1 HEAD, schema-valid Recorder manifests make the following exact: successfully archived invocation count and exact role counts from unambiguous CLI role flags, with all unknown/ambiguous roles in `unclassified`; accepted Judge `continue` Receipts after digest verification and package-contract validation; and stored accepted-Receipt byte lengths. Include `doctor` in the recognized role map. A failed/unarchived invocation, including the prior Issue #12 Judge attempt, is outside those recorded counts. Classify paper bytes as all verified accepted role Receipt bytes except Coder/Fixer invocations carrying an unambiguous `apply` phase; classify those as apply bytes. Emit the exact numerator/denominator pair rather than a rounded quotient, and report the byte ratio unavailable when no apply denominator exists or any admitted Receipt cannot be classified. Typed caller-supplied issue-open and merged-PR metadata can prove `issueToDefaultMerge` only when repository identity, issue identity, merged PR identity, default-base identity, and ordered timestamps all validate; otherwise it is unavailable. Current Recorder v1 records no invocation timestamps and only accepted audits, so `auditRejectionCount`, first/last `recordedInvocationWindow`, and `paperApplyWallClock` are unavailable with precise reasons. Do not infer them from paths, prose, commit cadence, sessions, or raw Pi events. Enumerate the committed docket tree, validate every candidate against the shipped manifest contract, verify referenced Receipt digest/length, reject corruption or duplicate invocation identity rather than silently skipping it, use stable path ordering/canonical serialization, and prove determinism in tests. One day is exactly 86,400,000 ms of owner calibration context for cross-case issue-to-default-merge trends; it is not serialized as a pass/fail result, SLA, law, threshold, scheduler, or trigger. Comparing current and previous lines is caller presentation and Doctor interpretation, not producer policy."
      },
      {
        "name": "doctor-evidence-intake",
        "owner": "The package-owned Doctor invocation-input contract and constrained evidence reader",
        "boundary": "A frozen, digest-bound examination snapshot. It admits the factory claim chain and normalized metadata while preventing the model from reaching sessions, product source, arbitrary files, or a live worktree.",
        "disposition": "Require a typed evidence index at activation. It binds repository and full committed target; a unique exact target catalog; admitted cross-case populations; and uniquely keyed evidence entries. The only target kinds are `law | gate | template | station | seat`, and targets must be active reusable factory artifacts. Preserve each caller-supplied target key byte-for-byte and compare it exactly without normalization. Case artifacts, comments, Receipts, manifests, dispositions, repairs, product behavior, and individual bugs are evidence or symptoms, not catalog targets. Admitted evidence is limited to digest-verified committed docket claim-chain artifacts (`manifest | receipt | verdict | disposition`), validated StatsLine records, normalized Git metadata limited to commit identity/timestamps/paths, and normalized tracker issue/PR identities/timestamps. Reject session payloads, raw Pi event streams, source blobs/diffs, live-worktree content, arbitrary prompt claims as evidence, and unknown evidence kinds. Give the Doctor a package evidence tool that reads only admitted evidence IDs, including bounded pagination, and no native `read`, `grep`, `find`, `ls`, `bash`, `Agent`, write, edit, or network tool. Maintain only an ephemeral read-coverage ledger for output validation/audit and discard it after the invocation; it is not durable Doctor memory or a second docket ledger. Invalid index shape, digest mismatch, target mismatch, duplicate identity, or inaccessible committed evidence fails activation honestly as infrastructure/contract failure. A valid but substantively insufficient admitted population may instead produce the lawful typed `refused` output."
      },
      {
        "name": "doctor-output-contract",
        "owner": "The package-owned `ak_doctor_output` contract and its structural validator",
        "boundary": "The sole legal result of one Doctor examination. It reports evidence and recommendations but neither edits law nor executes, routes, or approves a prescription.",
        "disposition": "Implement an exact closed discriminated union. `completed` requires a nonempty typed cross-case trend section, examination coverage keyed to catalog targets, and `findings` (which may be empty); it forbids refusal fields. Every trend cites at least two distinct validated StatsLines and joins each point exactly to the cited line, while allowing typed unavailable points to expose observability disease without fabricating a trend value. `refused` requires a nonblank reason and nonempty typed missing-evidence records and forbids coverage, trends, findings, and prescriptions. Every finding has one exact catalog target, admitted/read evidence citations, `disposition: keep | thin | delete`, typed answers to the three guardrail questions (reproducible failure, owning seam/invariant, and whether deletion or simplification suffices), a bounded prescription kind, and required `lastRealBite`. The actual branch cites an admitted/read docket `receipt | verdict` by sealed identity and exact target key. The no-bite branch repeats the exact target key, identifies its admitted population bound, and supplies the exact complete set of eligible Receipt/verdict evidence IDs; runtime must compare that set to the input population and require every member to have been fully read. It is tagged `noRealBite` and must never be rendered as an actual bite. Enforce mechanically that `keep` requires the actual-citation branch; `noRealBite` permits only `thin | delete`. Actual citations may still support any disposition. Enforce unique finding targets and exact joins among catalog, coverage, evidence, trends, and proof branches. Prescription kinds distinguish retain/delete/simplify from patch/mechanism addition; patch or mechanism addition requires a separate nonblank explanation of why deletion or simplification cannot achieve the health outcome. Recommendation text remains human-facing and is not parsed for state, target, evidence, or routing semantics. No four-reason field or bundled-law reference is present."
      },
      {
        "name": "doctor-role-runtime",
        "owner": "The Doctor role controller in the shared package role runtime",
        "boundary": "Single-invocation mechanics: activation, evidence-tool access, candidate validation, audit handoff, and termination. It has no inter-role or closure topology.",
        "disposition": "Add `doctor` to the exact `--ak-role` catalog, require the Doctor evidence input, load the bundled Doctor Soul, expose only the constrained evidence tool and `ak_doctor_output`, and inject the frozen catalog/index without exposing arbitrary filesystem paths. `ak_doctor_output` must be the sole final tool call. Before acceptance, validate all intrinsic state laws, evidence joins, full-read requirements, R1 proof completeness, and keep/no-bite legality. Then run the compliance audit; only a passing audit returns typed details and terminates. Audit revise remains a named resubmission error with no package retry loop or cap; transport/audit failure aborts honestly and never manufactures a refusal or Receipt. The runtime must not summon another role, prescribe a next role, know invocation order or count, schedule examinations, impose cadence/thresholds, query the tracker, alter closure, edit files, or retain cross-call memory."
      },
      {
        "name": "doctor-soul-audit",
        "owner": "The bundled Doctor Soul and the generalized same-model isolated Soul-compliance audit seam",
        "boundary": "Irreducible professional judgment only. Schema owns fields and states; runtime owns mechanics; caller overlay owns host law; examination evidence owns case facts.",
        "disposition": "Write a short Doctor Soul containing only: the factory/process patient boundary; evidence-only authority and prohibition on adjudicating/building/editing law; the examination distinction between an actual docket Receipt/verdict bite and a complete no-bite proof; and the preference for deletion/simplification over mechanisms or patches. Point to the package's existing canonical three-question guardrail doctrine without copying field mechanics. Do not include StatsLine field lists, tool-call rules, CLI flags, role ordering, refusal-state rules, one-day threshold logic, case names, first-examination prescriptions, or the host four-reason law. Generalize/reuse the existing fresh same-active-model isolated audit transport so Doctor audit sees Soul, frozen admitted evidence/read record, and proposed typed output and checks procedural compliance rather than replacing medical judgment. Preserve Judge behavior while adding Doctor-specific labels/input. Soul-content regression tests must prove necessary principles remain and schema/runtime/host details did not leak in."
      },
      {
        "name": "package-and-regression-surface",
        "owner": "Package extension wiring, public exports/distribution, usage documentation, and seam-owned tests",
        "boundary": "Makes the authorized StatsLine and Doctor contracts consumable and shippable without broadening their governance scope or repairing unrelated factory defects.",
        "disposition": "Wire loaders/dependencies through the shared extension, export the package-owned StatsLine/Doctor contract types and validators at the same public seam as existing roles, and ensure the npm artifact includes the Doctor Soul and every runtime/schema module it loads. Add README text only for invocation flags/input format and producer/consumer usage; do not use README as contract or design authority and do not undertake the existing README-law migration here. Add focused regressions for deterministic committed-snapshot stats; exact role/phase classification; corrupt/duplicate/unarchived exclusions; all measured/unavailable cases; tracker default-merge joins; R1 actual/no-bite and keep restrictions; complete population/full-read enforcement; exact target identity; completed/refused exclusivity; forbidden evidence/tool access; sole-final-call behavior; audit revise/failure honesty; active-tool narrowing; and packed-artifact loading. Existing role tests must remain green. Delete temporary probes after graduating each behavior once. Construction may proceed directly from this authority; no Plan artifact, Plan judgment, role ordering, or new workflow station is required or authorized."
      }
    ],
    "note": "Bounded validation at HEAD `71e592fd58b363ce1c0b97ad3b394014e673aaee` independently checked the candidate against merged `.ak/dockets/issues/12/authority/materials.md`, ADRs 0010 and 0012-0014, CONTEXT, owner comment 014, and the relevant current Recorder seams. R1 removes the no-bite expressibility contradiction, and L1 removes the Soul-layering/canonical-source contradiction. The candidate faithfully preserves the evidence-only factory Doctor, closure-produced single ledger, caller-owned composition and manual summoning, exact current StatsLine observability limits, and package-versus-caller boundaries. Its `continue` status is solely direct construction dispatch, not an Authority or Plan gate.\n\nThe admitted complete authority bundle's late-material dispositions remain controlling without reopening them: first-examination cases and later prescriptions do not authorize runner gates, README-law migration, memory policy, Fixer automation, capability preflight, issue slicing, or parallel execution here. #13 recurrence/failureClass, #22 orchestration, and #26 Recorder transport remain excluded. The prior accepted-but-unarchived tool lifecycle remains infrastructure evidence only, not a Receipt or authority."
  },
  "artifactKind": "acceptedReceipt"
}

